ng explains what's  happening there could be a warning  to the rest of the world they spend  hours draped head to toe  in white but for many health care  workers in brazil  their world is dark it's horrifying  to say the least when i arrived here in  mid-january i've seen a hospital that  normally had 20 beds only  or a small small facility and they had  at  this point almost 50 patients all of  them of it  and many of them died all the time fabio  biokini is the manaus field coordinator  for doctors without borders  in the first wave so many in the region  were sick it was believed more than half  of the population  had immunity then  re-infections occurred the p1 variant  might be the cause a preliminary  research paper suggests  p1 can be between 1.4 and 2.2 times  more transmissible than local non-p1  lineages  and can evade 25 to 61 percent of  protective  immunity elicited by previous infection  so it's a very scary situation  it's even more scary because you don't  have a conclusion yet  with a virus surging across brazil and  numerous hospitals on the brink of  collapse  this professor who studies disease  projection says  everyone is at risk we need to control  this virus as soon as possible  otherwise we will keep having new  variants that's what viruses do they  mutate all the time  and we risk having a mutation that will  be even  make the vaccine even less effective  vaccines are  still seen as the best route out of the  pandemic  the rollout in brazil has been slow  less than three and a half percent of  the population has received a single  dose  crystal glancing global news london  it's not only humans who are getting  vaccinated nine great apes at the san  diego zoo have been given an  experimental covid19 vaccine  four orangutans and five bonobos got the  shot earlier this year  it happened soon after a troop of  gorillas at the zoo became infected with  the virus  three more bonobos and a gorilla are  expected to get vaccinated soon  around the wo